[gb_interpret accounting and RAM fallback selection]
Ghidra: Instruction semantics are unchanged. This fixes host accounting on
existing branch/call/return exits; no unknown ROM routine is inferred.
Rationale: Every exit records the session once. LLE decodes actual instructions;
the historical RAM shortcuts are an explicit developer HLE build selection.
Generated dispatch checks AOT copied-code bodies first. Unmatched RAM enters
this accounted path, so dynamic shortcuts cannot masquerade as static coverage.

[RET/RETI stack timing]
Use the shared timed return for RET, taken RET cc and RETI. The two stack reads
follow the fetch/conditional idle cycles, matching SameBoy ret and ret_cc.
Total instruction cycles and one accounting exit are retained; partial hardware
ticks do not advance EI's instruction delay. See the always-on MMX2 dispatch
evidence and reference in gbrt.log.
